 [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Each|ea]]. [[Cookbook:Jalapeño|jalapeño]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 8 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]] [[Cookbook:Tempeh|tempeh]] or ground [[Cookbook:Beef|beef]]\n* 2 tbsp [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] cooked [[Cookbook:Rice|jasmine rice]]\n* 1 medium kabocha [[Cookbook:Squash|squash]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Cut off top of kabocha squash and scoop out seeds.\n# [[Cookbook:Baking|Bake]] the squash for 45 minutes at 375°F (190°C) or until a sharp knife goes through the flesh easily.\n# Meanwhile, [[Cookbook:Frying|fry]] the tempeh, shallots, ginger, and jalapeño. Cook until tempeh is completely brown, and then add soy sauce and rice. Take off heat and [[Cookbook:Mixing|mix]] thoroughly.\n# Put tempeh mixture into kabocha squash and bake for 30 more minutes.\n\n[[Category:Vegan recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using squash]]\n[[Category:Recipes for stuffing and dressing]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using tempeh]]\n[[Category:Recipes using peanut oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using jalapeño chile]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Stuffed Kabocha Squash","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 tbsp peanut oil","sourceText":"4 tbsp peanut oil","amountText":"4 tbsp peanut oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 tbsp chopped shallots","sourceText":"2 tbsp chopped shallots","amountText":"2 tbsp chopped shallots","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"1-inch piece chopped ginger","sourceText":"1-inch piece chopped ginger","amountText":"1-inch piece chopped ginger","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 ea. jalapeño, chopped","sourceText":"1 ea. jalapeño, chopped","amountText"